WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.910
A liquid medication used to always come in a
bottle and you had to pour your dose with a

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.040
steady hand into a spoon.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:13.430
Today, many medications and supplements come
inside small food, safe casings that are easy

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.110
to swallow and portable.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.090
Soft gel capsules.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:22.520
Many types of products come in gel capsules
from prescription drugs to health supplements

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.930
such as fish oils.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.010
Many of these medicine fills go bad if
exposed to oxygen.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.140
So the gel cap, besides being convenient,
also serves as a protective barrier.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:38.930
Every ingredient in both the gel cap and the
medicine fill inside undergoes extensive

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.310
testing for purity.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.310
The first test phase checks for bacterial
contamination.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.880
Lab technicians dissolve the ingredient in
solution.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:53.060
Apply it to a food source in a petri dish,
then incubate the dish for 72 hours to

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.700
encourage any existing bacteria to grow.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.420
Then they draw samples and examine them
under a microscope.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:04.680
If those samples are bacteria free, the
ingredient moves onto the second phase of

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:10.380
testing, which checks for contaminants such
as lead, arsenic, mercury and cadmium.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:17.040
This machine, called a spectrometer, injects
the ingredient solution into a plasma flame.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.060
Then, by reading the changes in light
wavelengths, analyzes the chemical

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:26.010
composition. If the ingredient is
contaminant free, it gets the go ahead.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:33.240
The gel cap is made entirely of natural
ingredients gelatin derived from beef bones,

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.780
palm oil, glycerin and purified water.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.240
The proportions are top secret.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.160
An industrial blender combines the three
ingredients to a uniform.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.270
Consistency then heats the mixture to 80°C.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.570
A vacuum sucks out the air bubbles.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.630
As this now ready gel material flows into a
holding tank.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:00.120
Simultaneously, they prepare the medicine
fill, in this case vitamin D.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:05.490
They combine it with soybean oil to adjust
the potency to the specified strength.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:11.970
Meanwhile, they maintain the gel cap
material in the holding tank at 60°C to

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.430
prevent it from prematurely solidifying.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:20.520
Even the hose leaving that tank is wrapped
in heater tape to keep the gel liquid a

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.870
separate hose. Feeds the vitamin D solution
from another holding tank down to the

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.290
production floor as well.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:32.310
This hose doesn't require heating because
vitamin D and soybean oil don't solidify when

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:38.880
cool. On the production line, two stations
simultaneously spread a thin layer of molten

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.680
gel across a cooling drum.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:46.470
The gel hardens into a solid yet malleable
sheet about the thickness of cardboard.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:53.100
Each sheet passes over a rotating die with
capsule shaped cavities just before the two

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.540
gel sheets come together.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.280
Pumps inject the required quantity of
vitamin D solution into each cavity.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:04.740
The pressure pushing the gelatin into the
cavity at the same time the machine heats the

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.690
gel sheets so that when they meet, they
adhere to each other, forming full capsules

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.540
with the vitamin D solution sealed inside.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:18.630
In the final second, the dies sharp edges
slice the gel caps free and they fall to a

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.040
conveyor belt below.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:25.980
At this point, the filled gel caps contain a
fair bit of moisture, so they're quite soft.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.440
If they'd lay on a surface too long, they'd
flatten.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:33.870
So the conveyor belt whisks them very
quickly into a rotating drum where they

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.920
tumble in slightly cool, dry air for about
three hours.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:43.380
This removes enough moisture to make the gel
caps hard enough to lie on a surface without

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:50.100
flattening. After exiting the gel, caps move
into a second dryer where spread out on

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.950
trays. This time they dry for about 36
hours.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.900
After that, the gel caps are hard enough to
be safely packaged.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:06.030
The gel caps, the ones being packaged here,
contain flax oil, travel down a series of

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.050
vibrating plates which progressively line
them up in single file.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:16.920
As they pass by, electronic eyes count out
the number of capsules per bottle, triggering

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.630
the filling mechanism to collect that
quantity and release it into an empty bottle.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.510
The next station applies a plastic twist
cap.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:37.880
Then the bottles move onward, each one
plowing directly into the center of an

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:44.570
adhesive backed label, which rollers then
apply around the sides before shipping The

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:50.090
quality control lab tests random samples
from the production batch to verify that the

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.820
gel caps meet all specifications.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:05:00.650
It's a playground staple, a stationary ride
on cartoon animal that bounces up and down

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:06.050
and rocks back and forth courtesy of a huge
spring underneath secured into the ground.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:10.770
The bouncy coil base is what gives this type
of playground equipment its name.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.080
A Spring Rider.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:18.680
The Spring Rider is a playground favorite to
withstand years of rambunctious riders.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.990
It has to be solid and durable.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:25.610
Yet for a toddler to be able to rock back
and forth, it can't be too heavy.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:31.020
That's why the spring is made of thick steel
and the animal of lightweight aluminum.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:38.200
That sand core is comprised of two halves,
each made with an aluminum mold duct shaped.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:44.890
In this case, workers fill it with sand and
adhesive mix that sets into a solid block.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:54.070
They insert several steel support rods, fill
to the top and even out the surface, then

00:05:54.070 --> 00:06:00.040
expose two hooks they'll grab to extract the
core half once the sand hardens in about 20

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:06.390
minutes. Meanwhile, other workers use an
aluminum pattern to make each half of the

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.770
duct casting mold.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:13.140
After applying a powder release agent to
prevent sticking, they cover the pattern with

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.660
a sieved mixture of sand and clay.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.470
They mount a frame around the pattern to
contain the sand as they add more and more

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.370
repeatedly packing it down in all areas with
a pneumatic ramming tool.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.790
Then they removed the frame and cover the
sand with a wooden board.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:39.100
This provides a hard surface for the press,
which now applies the weight of about four

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.810
mid-size SUVs.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:46.540
Then they flip the mold over and remove the
pattern which formed the mold cavity.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:50.890
The sand is now so firmly compacted that it
holds the shape.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.440
One half of the sand mold has channels
through which the molten metal will flow into

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:02.350
the cavity. Workers now position several six
millimeter thick foam spacers in the cavity

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.810
and place half of the core on top of them.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:11.020
The spacers elevate the core, creating a six
millimeter cavity between core and mold.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.080
The other half of the core goes on top.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:21.220
After placing spacers on top of that to
create a six millimeter gap on this side as

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.580
well, they carefully lower the other half of
the sand mold.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.580
Now they're ready to cast the duck.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.730
The melting point of aluminum is 590°C.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:39.070
However, they heat it much higher to 760
degrees, so it'll flow faster and fill the

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.040
entire cavity before beginning to solidify.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.750
They pour the metal through holes on top.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.500
It flows through the runners into the mold
cavity, which is that six millimeter gap

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.420
surrounding the duck shaped core.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:57.430
About 20 minutes later, the metal has cooled
and solidified.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.710
They break the mold apart on a vibrating
sieve, releasing the aluminum duck and

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.550
shaking out the core sand through a hole at
the bottom of the duck.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:11.920
After cutting off excess aluminum that
hardened in the runners, they grind down the

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.350
seam, which formed in between the two halves
of the mold.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:21.770
Next, they weld on aluminum handles for the
child to grip when riding.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:26.210
These handles are cast in sand molds just
like the duck.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:33.710
Workers grind down the weld and any sharp
edges, making the entire surface nice and

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:38.360
smooth. Next.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:41.630
A coat of polyester powder in bright rubber
ducky.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:50.500
Yellow. Then a 20 minute trip through an
oven to bake the coating, making it ultra

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:58.570
durable. Now delicately airbrushed with a
urethane enamel paint the details that bring

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.890
Mr. Duck to life.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.130
His feet, wings, bill and eyes.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:09.670
The thick coil that makes this a spring
rider is made of a flexible type of steel.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.330
They bolt a steel spacer plate to it.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.470
Then hide the bolts under an aluminum cover.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:28.060
After attaching a footrest steel again, they
bolt the duct to the plate.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:34.630
All these parts like the duck are painted
with baked on polyester coating.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.650
The spring bolts to a concrete block buried
underground.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:45.100
Ducky and friends are designed to withstand
even the harshest winters, letting children

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.950
enjoy a little spring all year round.

